# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Inkflow has NO build step — .env variables are NOT read at runtime.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# This file exists only to document where API keys actually come from.
# It is safe to delete.
#
# How to configure AI providers (OpenRouter / Anthropic / Ollama):
#
#   1. Open the app (index.html) and open the AI panel in the sidebar.
#   2. Pick a provider, choose a model, and paste your key into the
#      "API Key" field:
#        OpenRouter  → sk-or-v1-…   (https://openrouter.ai/keys)
#        Anthropic   → sk-ant-api-… (https://console.anthropic.com)
#        Ollama      → no key needed; set the endpoint host instead.
#   3. Optionally tick "Remember key" — the key is then stored in your
#      browser's localStorage under:
#        inkflow-api-key-openrouter
#        inkflow-api-key-anthropic
#
# Keys are sent only to the selected provider's API endpoint and never
# to any other server. Do not commit real keys anywhere in this repo.
